---
title: Sticky Prawns with Veg-Packed Egg Fried Rice
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Chinese
---

Rinse and cook the @rice{250%g}(jasmine or long grain). When cooked rinse thoroughly under cold water to remove any starch. Set aside to cool.

Heat 1 tablespoon of @sesame oil{5%tbsp} in a #large wok{}. Fry the @raw king prawns{330%g} on a medium-high heat for 1 or ~{2%minutes} on each side, until just turned pink. Transfer to a plate or bowl and set aside for later.

Return the wok to a high heat and add 2 tablespoons of sesame oil. Fry the white parts of the @spring onions{6} and the @mixed stir fry vegetables{330%g} for ~{2%minutes} to soften.

Add the rice and 2 tablespoons of @soy sauce{3%tbsp}. Cook this mixture for ~{2%minutes}, stirring often to coat the rice with the soy sauce.

Move the rice and vegetables to the sides of the wok. Add a drizzle of oil and pour in the @eggs{4}(beaten). Leave for a ~{1%minute} before beating again, then stir vigorously through the rice so that the egg breaks up among the grains.

Add @salt{pinch} and most of the green sliced spring onions (reserving a handful for garnish) to the pan, then turn the heat down very low.

In a clean #frying pan{}, heat another tablespoon of oil over a medium-high heat. Add the @garlic{3%cloves}(finely grated) and @ginger{25%g}(peeled and finely chopped). Cook for ~{2%minutes}, stirring so it does not burn, until just beginning to colour.

Add the @sriracha{3%tbsp}(or other hot sauce), @honey{1%tsp}, and remaining soy sauce. Let it all sizzle for a few minutes, stirring occasionally, until looking sticky.

Add the prawns to the sauce and gently shake the pan to coat. Once coated, turn down the heat.

Divide the egg fried rice between 4 bowls and top each one with the sticky glazed prawns, a sprinkling of @sesame seeds{}, a splash of soy sauce and sriracha, then the remaining green spring onion slices.